  "notes": "Contract written during the 2026-09-27 MDN-shape upgrade, which also corrected the previous revision's model: it said the page's Document Policy 'now applies to workers spawned by that page', but the explainer's proposed solution is the opposite for network workers \u2014 the worker script's own response header is authoritative and 'any creator policy is ignored'; only blob:/data: workers clone the creator. Chrome 147's trial covers dedicated workers; the explainer's shared/service-worker semantics are described as the proposal's scope, not as shipped Chrome behavior. Runtime behavior is source-derived, not executed locally."
